I have some ideas for some later versions of nethack. I'm posting them here
in the almost certainly vain hope that a NH developer may read it....
I've got a couple of ideas for later versions of nethack.
Firstly...
One thing that _really_ pisses me off is when you're starving to death
(or maybe being chased by something nasty) and you're stuck in a corridor
with a cat/dog that just INSISTs on getting in your way, thus causing you
to starve to death/get beaten up. I think it would be great if you could
kick/otherwise attack your pet, with the following possible results:

a) Pet keeps out of your way for a while, returns later.
b) Pet becomes wild, has to be retamed.
c) Pet gets really pissed off and attacks you.
d) Any nearby monsters leap to defend your poor innocent pet and beat the
   crap out of you.

Possibly get aggravate monster intrinsic too.
It has been suggested this should only happen with cats, dogs should be
undyingly faithful.


Second idea (much less practical and sillier...)
Characters could have long names. I get fed up with just 'Gurfleblap',
'Flarbobutt', or 'Huuuurgh' (my characters' various names.).
What would be nice is if you had a short name (on screen name), and
a longer, formal name, such as...

Gurfleblap of Froobnitz, Protector of Snozbarf, Keeper of the Green Sponge,
 Destroyer of the Termites of Doom, Stirrer of the Gnomish Frog-soup.

One criticism that has been made of this idea, is where the hell can you put
such a name? (i.e not scorelist, not during game, so when?)

